<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n6664" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀνακᾰλυπτήρια</span></b> , τά,
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>festival of unveiling,</i>
			when the bride first took off her maiden veil, and received presents
			from the bridegroom, <i><span class="en">
				Poll.
				3.36
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Timae.
				149
			</span></i>, Hsch.s. v.sq. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>the presents themselves,</i> subject of a speech attributed to
			Lysias, <i><span class="en">
				Theon
				<u>Prog.</u>
				2
			</span></i>: in sg., <i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				<u>Tim.</u>
				8
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>III.</b>
			<i>revelations,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Ph.
				1.358
			</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
    <div class="alpheios-lex-alph-source">From <u>
            <u>A Greek-English Lexicon</u>
        </u> (Henry George Liddell, Robert Scott, Oxford, Clarendon Press, 1940) </div>
